      {
        "id": "u1",
        "kind": "CONCEPT",
        "label": "Atomic structure and atomic number as chemical identity",
        "attributes": {
          "depth": "explanation"
        },
        "subtopic_ids": [
          "s1"
        ],
        "rationale": "Reviews basic subatomic particles (protons, neutrons, electrons) and explains that the atomic number Z (number of protons) exclusively determines the identity of a chemical element.",
        "review_flags": [],
        "contextualization": {
          "value": "none",
          "evidence": []
        },
        "passages": [
          {
            "id": "p1",
            "category": "ORGANIZATION",
            "attributes": {
              "subtype": "social"
            },
            "formats": [
              "prose"
            ],
            "review_flags": [],
            "text": "Bonjour ! Installe-toi, tu vas voir que la notion d'**isotope**, c’est en fait très visuel et beaucoup plus simple qu'il n'y paraît. ",
            "start": 0,
            "end": 133
          },
          {
            "id": "p2",
            "category": "ORGANIZATION",
            "attributes": {
              "subtype": "structural"
            },
            "formats": [
              "prose"
            ],
            "review_flags": [],
            "text": "Pour bien comprendre, faisons un tout petit rappel sur l'atome, et ensuite, je te donne une métaphore.",
            "start": 135,
            "end": 237
          },
          {
            "id": "p3",
            "category": "ORGANIZATION",
            "attributes": {
              "subtype": "structural"
            },
            "formats": [
              "separator"
            ],
            "review_flags": [],
            "text": "---",
            "start": 239,
            "end": 242
          },
          {
            "id": "p4",
            "category": "ORGANIZATION",
            "attributes": {
              "subtype": "structural"
            },
            "formats": [
              "heading"
            ],
            "review_flags": [],
            "text": "### 1. Le petit rappel : La \"carte d'identité\" de l'atome",
            "start": 244,
            "end": 301
          },
          {
            "id": "p5",
            "category": "CONCEPT",
            "attributes": {
              "depth": "statement"
            },
            "formats": [
              "prose"
            ],
            "review_flags": [],
            "text": "Dans un atome, tu as un noyau au centre avec :",
            "start": 303,
            "end": 349
          },
          {
            "id": "p6",
            "category": "CONCEPT",
            "attributes": {
              "depth": "statement"
            },
            "formats": [
              "list",
              "prose"
            ],
            "review_flags": [],
            "text": "*   Des **protons** (chargés positivement).",
            "start": 350,
            "end": 393
          },
          {
            "id": "p7",
            "category": "CONCEPT",
            "attributes": {
              "depth": "statement"
            },
            "formats": [
              "list",
              "prose"
            ],
            "review_flags": [],
            "text": "*   Des **neutrons** (neutres, pas de charge).",
            "start": 394,
            "end": 440
          },
          {
            "id": "p8",
            "category": "CONCEPT",
            "attributes": {
              "depth": "statement"
            },
            "formats": [
              "prose"
            ],
            "review_flags": [],
            "text": "Et autour, des **électrons** qui tournent.",
            "start": 441,
            "end": 483
          },
          {
            "id": "p9",
            "category": "CONCEPT",
            "attributes": {
              "depth": "explanation"
            },
            "formats": [
              "prose"
            ],
            "review_flags": [],
            "text": "Ce qui définit un élément chimique (le carbone, l'or, l'oxygène...), c'est **UNIQUEMENT son nombre de protons** (noté **$Z$**, le numéro atomique). ",
            "start": 485,
            "end": 633
          },
          {
            "id": "p10",
            "category": "CONCEPT",
            "attributes": {
              "depth": "explanation"
            },
            "formats": [
              "list",
              "prose"
            ],
            "review_flags": [],
            "text": "* C'est sa carte d'identité : si un atome a 6 protons, c'est **toujours** du carbone. S'il en a 7, c'est de l'azote. Tu ne peux pas changer le nombre de protons sans changer d'élément.",
            "start": 634,
            "end": 818
          }
        ],
        "accuracy": {
          "verdict": "accurate",
          "reason": "The descriptions of subatomic particles and the role of the atomic number Z in defining an element are scientifically accurate.",
          "errors": []
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "u2",
        "kind": "ANALOGY",
        "label": "Identical twins with backpacks metaphor",
        "attributes": {},
        "subtopic_ids": [
          "s2"
        ],
        "rationale": "Introduces an everyday analogy comparing isotopes to identical twins carrying backpacks of differing weights.",
        "review_flags": [],
        "contextualization": {
          "value": "everyday",
          "evidence": [
            {
              "passage_id": "p12",
              "quote": "Imagine des jumeaux identiques. Ils ont exactement le même visage, le même ADN, le même nom de famille. Mais l'un d'eux a un sac à dos un peu plus lourd que l'autre. "
            }
          ]
        },
        "passages": [
          {
            "id": "p11",
            "category": "ORGANIZATION",
            "attributes": {
              "subtype": "structural"
            },
            "formats": [
              "heading"
            ],
            "review_flags": [],
            "text": "### 2. Alors, c'est quoi un isotope ? (La métaphore des jumeaux)",
            "start": 820,
            "end": 884
          },
          {
            "id": "p12",
            "category": "ANALOGY",
            "attributes": {},
            "formats": [
              "prose"
            ],
            "review_flags": [],
            "text": "Imagine des jumeaux identiques. Ils ont exactement le même visage, le même ADN, le même nom de famille. Mais l'un d'eux a un sac à dos un peu plus lourd que l'autre. ",
            "start": 886,
            "end": 1052
          }
        ],
        "accuracy": {
          "verdict": "accurate",
          "reason": "The analogy accurately captures the concept that isotopes share the same core chemical identity while differing in mass.",
          "errors": []
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "u3",
        "kind": "CONCEPT",
        "label": "Definition of isotopes",
        "attributes": {
          "depth": "explanation"
        },
        "subtopic_ids": [
          "s2"
        ],
        "rationale": "Provides the conceptual and formal definition of isotopes as atoms having the same atomic number Z but different mass numbers A due to different neutron counts.",
        "review_flags": [],
        "contextualization": {
          "value": "none",
          "evidence": []
        },
        "passages": [
          {
            "id": "p13",
            "category": "CONCEPT",
            "attributes": {
              "depth": "statement"
            },
            "formats": [
              "prose"
            ],
            "review_flags": [],
            "text": "**Les isotopes, ce sont des atomes \"jumeaux\" :**",
            "start": 1054,
            "end": 1102
          },
          {
            "id": "p14",
            "category": "CONCEPT",
            "attributes": {
              "depth": "explanation"
            },
            "formats": [
              "list",
              "prose"
            ],
            "review_flags": [],
            "text": "* Ils ont le **même nombre de protons** (donc c'est le même élément chimique).",
            "start": 1103,
            "end": 1181
          },
          {
            "id": "p15",
            "category": "CONCEPT",
            "attributes": {
              "depth": "statement"
            },
            "formats": [
              "list",
              "prose"
            ],
            "review_flags": [],
            "text": "* Mais ils ont un **nombre de neutrons différent**.",
            "start": 1182,
            "end": 1233
          },
          {
            "id": "p16",
            "category": "CONCEPT",
            "attributes": {
              "depth": "explanation"
            },
            "formats": [
              "prose"
            ],
            "review_flags": [],
            "text": "Comme les neutrons pèsent lourd, l'un des atomes sera simplement plus lourd que l'autre !",
            "start": 1235,
            "end": 1324
          },
          {
            "id": "p17",
            "category": "ORGANIZATION",
            "attributes": {
              "subtype": "structural"
            },
            "formats": [
              "prose"
            ],
            "review_flags": [],
            "text": "> **La définition officielle à retenir pour tes contrôles :** ",
            "start": 1326,
            "end": 1388
          },
          {
            "id": "p18",
            "category": "CONCEPT",
            "attributes": {
              "depth": "statement"
            },
            "formats": [
              "prose"
            ],
            "review_flags": [],
            "text": "> Des isotopes sont des atomes qui ont le **même numéro atomique $Z$** (même nombre de protons), mais un **nombre de masse $A$ différent** (nombre de neutrons différent).",
            "start": 1389,
            "end": 1559
          }
        ],
        "accuracy": {
          "verdict": "accurate",
          "reason": "The definition of isotopes (same Z, different A) and explanation of the mass difference from neutrons are standard and accurate.",
          "errors": []
        }
      },
