            ],
            "review_flags": [],
            "text": "### 3. L'exemple classique : Le Carbone",
            "start": 1566,
            "end": 1605
          },
          {
            "id": "p21",
            "category": "CONCEPT",
            "attributes": {
              "depth": "statement"
            },
            "formats": [
              "prose"
            ],
            "review_flags": [],
            "text": "Dans la nature, le carbone existe sous plusieurs formes (isotopes). Les deux plus connus sont :",
            "start": 1607,
            "end": 1702
          },
          {
            "id": "p22",
            "category": "EXAMPLE",
            "attributes": {},
            "formats": [
              "list",
              "prose"
            ],
            "review_flags": [],
            "text": "1.  **Le Carbone 12 ($^{12}\\text{C}$) :** C'est le plus courant (99 % du carbone sur Terre).",
            "start": 1704,
            "end": 1796
          },
          {
            "id": "p23",
            "category": "EXAMPLE",
            "attributes": {},
            "formats": [
              "list"
            ],
            "review_flags": [],
            "text": "    *   6 protons",
            "start": 1797,
            "end": 1814
          },
          {
            "id": "p24",
            "category": "EXAMPLE",
            "attributes": {},
            "formats": [
              "list"
            ],
            "review_flags": [],
            "text": "    *   **6 neutrons**",
            "start": 1815,
            "end": 1837
          },
          {
            "id": "p25",
            "category": "EXAMPLE",
            "attributes": {},
            "formats": [
              "equation",
              "list"
            ],
            "review_flags": [],
            "text": "    *   Masse totale ($A$) = 6 + 6 = **12**",
            "start": 1838,
            "end": 1881
          },
          {
            "id": "p26",
            "category": "EXAMPLE",
            "attributes": {},
            "formats": [
              "list",
              "prose"
            ],
            "review_flags": [],
            "text": "2.  **Le Carbone 14 ($^{14}\\text{C}$) :** Tu en as sûrement entendu parler pour dater les fossiles !",
            "start": 1883,
            "end": 1983
          },
          {
            "id": "p27",
            "category": "EXAMPLE",
            "attributes": {},
            "formats": [
              "list",
              "prose"
            ],
            "review_flags": [],
            "text": "    *   Toujours 6 protons (sinon ce ne serait plus du carbone !)",
            "start": 1984,
            "end": 2049
          },
          {
            "id": "p28",
            "category": "EXAMPLE",
            "attributes": {},
            "formats": [
              "list",
              "prose"
            ],
            "review_flags": [],
            "text": "    *   **8 neutrons** (il a deux neutrons de plus dans son \"sac à dos\")",
            "start": 2050,
            "end": 2122
          },
          {
            "id": "p29",
            "category": "EXAMPLE",
            "attributes": {},
            "formats": [
              "equation",
              "list"
            ],
            "review_flags": [],
            "text": "    *   Masse totale ($A$) = 6 + 8 = **14**",
            "start": 2123,
            "end": 2166
          }
        ],
        "accuracy": {
          "verdict": "accurate",
          "reason": "The proton and neutron counts and mass numbers for Carbon-12 and Carbon-14, as well as the abundance figure for Carbon-12 (~99%), are correct.",
          "errors": []
        }
